  "notes": "{祝|いわ}う is a godan verb meaning to celebrate an occasion or congratulate someone on an achievement.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: ～を{祝|いわ}う (to celebrate something)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {誕生日|たんじょうび}を{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate a birthday\n- {結婚|けっこん}を{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate a marriage\n- {合格|ごうかく}を{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate passing an exam\n- {成功|せいこう}を{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate a success\n- {新年|しんねん}を{祝|いわ}う: to celebrate the new year\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- お{祝|いわ}い: celebration; congratulatory gift (noun form with honorific お)\n- {祝日|しゅくじつ}: national holiday\n- {祝|しゅく}{福|ふく}: blessing, benediction\n\nNOTE:\nお{祝|いわ}いを{言|い}う means to offer congratulations. お{祝|いわ}い can also refer to the gift or money given on a celebratory occasion.",
